We investigate the existence of ground solutions in weighted Hölder spaces for the given biharmonic Choquard equation under exponential growth constraints. Our analysis considers the scenario described by the equation \begin{align*}
  \begin{split}
  \left(\mathcal{L}^2\mathcal{L}^2+\mathcal{L}^4\right)(u)=|x|^{-\alpha}*\left(e^{u}+\lambda h\right],
  \end{split}
  \end{align*} subject to zero boundary conditions and appropriate functional constraints. Our study reveals the existence of a standardized ground solution for this equation.
